---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Zen Aesthetic Clock">
  <!-- Dynamic Blobs Background -->
  <div class="fixed inset-0 z-[-2] bg-canvas overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center transition-colors duration-1000" id="bg-container">
    <div class="absolute w-[60vw] h-[60vw] max-w-[800px] max-h-[800px] bg-[#00ffff] opacity-30 dark:opacity-20 rounded-full blur-[100px] animate-blob-1" id="blob1"></div>
    <div class="absolute w-[50vw] h-[50vw] max-w-[700px] max-h-[700px] bg-[#ff00ff] opacity-30 dark:opacity-20 rounded-full blur-[100px] animate-blob-2" id="blob2"></div>
    <div class="absolute w-[55vw] h-[55vw] max-w-[750px] max-h-[750px] bg-[#ffff00] opacity-30 dark:opacity-20 rounded-full blur-[100px] animate-blob-3" id="blob3"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- Header Navigation -->
  <header class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-6 flex items-center justify-between z-10 relative">
    <a href="/" class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-ink font-semibold tracking-tight text-sm hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
      <span>Zen Aesthetic Clock</span>
    </a>
    <nav class="flex items-center space-x-4">
      <a href="/about" class="text-sm text-body hover:text-ink font-semibold transition-colors">About</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="text-sm text-body hover:text-ink font-semibold transition-colors">Contact</a>
      <a href="/privacy" class="text-sm text-ink font-bold transition-colors">Privacy</a>
      <a href="/terms" class="text-sm text-body hover:text-ink font-semibold transition-colors">Terms</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <!-- Main Content Area -->
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 z-10 relative">
    <!-- Back Button -->
    <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center space-x-2 text-xs text-mute hover:text-ink transition-colors mb-8 group">
      <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="transform group-hover:-translate-x-0.5 transition-transform"><line x1="19" y1="12" x2="5" y2="12"/><polyline points="12 19 5 12 12 5"/></svg>
      <span>Back to Clock</span>
    </a>

    <!-- Glassmorphic Content Card -->
    <article class="bg-canvas-soft/80 backdrop-blur-md border border-hairline rounded-lg p-8 md:p-12 shadow-lg select-text">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-8">Privacy Policy</h1>
      
      <div class="prose prose-sm dark:prose-invert max-w-none space-y-6 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
        <p>
          At Zen Aesthetic Clock, accessible from <a href="https://aestheticclock.com" class="text-link hover:underline">aestheticclock.com</a>, one of our main priorities is the privacy of our visitors. This Privacy Policy document contains types of information that is collected and recorded by Zen Aesthetic Clock and how we use it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Log Files</h2>
        <p>
          Zen Aesthetic Clock follows a standard procedure of using log files. These files log visitors when they visit websites. All hosting companies do this and a part of hosting services' analytics. The information collected by log files include internet protocol (IP) addresses, browser type, Internet Service Provider (ISP), date and time stamp, referring/exit pages, and possibly the number of clicks. These are not linked to any information that is personally identifiable. The purpose of the information is for analyzing trends, administering the site, tracking users' movement on the website, and gathering demographic information.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Cookies and Web Beacons</h2>
        <p>
          Like any other website, Zen Aesthetic Clock uses "cookies". These cookies are used to store information including visitors' preferences, and the pages on the website that the visitor accessed or visited. The information is used to optimize the users' experience by customizing our web page content based on visitors' browser type and/or other information.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Google DoubleClick DART Cookie</h2>
        <p>
          Google is one of a third-party vendor on our site. It also uses cookies, known as DART cookies, to serve ads to our site visitors based upon their visit to our site and other sites on the internet. However, visitors may choose to decline the use of DART cookies by visiting the Google ad and content network Privacy Policy at the following URL – <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link hover:underline">https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Advertising Partners Privacy Policies</h2>
        <p>
          Third-party ad servers or ad networks uses technologies like cookies, JavaScript, or Web Beacons that are used in their respective advertisements and links that appear on Zen Aesthetic Clock, which are sent directly to users' browser. They automatically receive your IP address when this occurs. These technologies are used to measure the effectiveness of their advertising campaigns and/or to personalize the advertising content that you see on websites that you visit.
        </p>
        <p class="text-mute text-xs">
          Note that Zen Aesthetic Clock has no access to or control over these cookies that are used by third-party advertisers.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Local Storage and Cookie Usage</h2>
        <p>
          We use local browser storage (such as <code>localStorage</code>) and cookies to save your interface configurations. This includes your preferred theme (dark or light mode), display preferences, and the link to your last-entered YouTube background focus video. Storing this information locally allows the application to automatically reload your preferred background audio and settings on future visits without requiring you to re-paste the URL. This data remains entirely on your device and is never uploaded to our servers or shared with third parties.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mt-8">Consent</h2>
        <p>
          By using our website, you hereby consent to our Privacy Policy and agree to its terms.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer Navigation -->
  <footer class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-8 border-t border-hairline text-center text-xs text-mute z-10 relative">
    <div class="flex justify-center space-x-6 mb-4">
      <a href="/about" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">About Us</a>
      <a href="/contact" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">Contact Us</a>
      <a href="/privacy" class="text-ink font-semibold transition-colors">Privacy Policy</a>
      <a href="/terms" class="hover:text-ink transition-colors">Terms & Conditions</a>
    </div>
    <p>&copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} Zen Aesthetic Clock. All rights reserved.</p>
  </footer>

  <script>
    // Randomize background blob starting positions on load
    const blobs = [document.getElementById('blob1'), document.getElementById('blob2'), document.getElementById('blob3')];
    const animationDurations = [25, 30, 35];
    blobs.forEach((blob, index) => {
      if (blob) {
        const duration = animationDurations[index];
        const randomDelay = Math.random() * -duration;
        blob.style.animationDelay = `${randomDelay}s`;
      }
    });
  </script>
</Layout>
